{"metadata":{"name":"Sunan Abu Dawud","section":{"33":{"eng-name":"Hot Baths (Kitab Al-Hammam)","ara-name":"كتاب الحمَّام"}},"section_detail":{"33":{"hadithnumber_first":4009,"hadithnumber_last":4019,"arabicnumber_first":4009,"arabicnumber_last":4019}}},"hadiths":[{"hadithnumber":4015,"arabicnumber":4015,"text":"Rapporté par Ali ibn Abu Talib رضي الله عنه : Le Prophète ﷺ a dit : « Ne découvre pas ta cuisse, et ne regarde pas la cuisse d’une personne vivante ou morte. » Abu Dawud a dit : Cette tradition diffère des traditions généralement rapportées (nakarah)","grades":[{"name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Very Daif"},{"name":"Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid","grade":"Very Daif"},{"name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Daif"}],"reference":{"book":33,"hadith":7},"chapter":{"id":2,"ara-name":"باب النَّهْىِ عَنِ التَّعَرِّي","eng-name":"The prohibition of nudity","isFirstHadith":false}}]}